    "text": "Save Small deletes a ring's render mesh.",
    "gold": [
      "Save Small"
    ]
  },
  "end": {
    "line": "Renders made with",
    "handle": "HeyGema"
  },
  "lines": [
    {
      "text": "Save Small deletes a ring's render mesh.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "compare",
        "before": "signet-cad.webp",
        "after": "signet-render.webp"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Before Rhino shades or renders a surface, it makes a mesh.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "title",
        "text": "Render mesh",
        "sub": "Surfaces as polygons"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Rhino saves that render mesh inside the .3dm file.",
      "say": "Rhino saves that render mesh inside the three D M file.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "photo",
        "src": "signet-cad.webp",
        "label": "Shaded in Rhino",
        "focus": {
          "x": 0.45,
          "y": 0.4,
          "k": 1.4
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Save Small leaves it out to make the file smaller.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "steps",
        "items": [
          "Save",
          "Save Small"
        ],
        "active": 1,
        "label": "Two ways to save"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Rhino rebuilds it when the file opens, so it shades more slowly.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "photo",
        "src": "eternity-cad.webp",
        "label": "Opened again",
        "focus": {
          "x": 0.5,
          "y": 0.5,
          "k": 1.3
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Other programs that read the saved mesh can find parts missing.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "reveal",
        "item": "empty",
        "openAt": 0.1,
        "stamp": "Missing",
        "stampAt": 0.9,
        "label": "No render mesh"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "A file only ever seen in wireframe has no render mesh either.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "title",
        "text": "Wireframe",
        "sub": "No render mesh"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Wireframe draws just curves and edges, with no shaded surface.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "steps",
        "items": [
          "Wireframe",
          "Shaded",
          "Rendered"
        ],
        "active": 0,
        "label": "Rhino display modes"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "The fix is to switch to Shaded, then save the normal way.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "steps",
        "items": [
          "Wireframe",
          "Shaded",
          "Rendered"
        ],
        "active": 1,
        "label": "Rhino display modes"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "With every surface shaded, every stone made it into this render.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "compare",
        "before": "cad-wireframe.webp",
        "after": "cad-render.webp"
      }
    }
  ],
  "post": {
    "youtube_title": "Jewelry rendering mistakes: Rhino's Save Small and wireframe",
    "caption": "Rhino turns surfaces into a render mesh to shade them and saves it in the .3dm file. Save Small leaves that mesh out, and a file only ever seen in wireframe has none, so set a viewport to Shaded and save with plain Save. The renders in this video were made with HeyGema.",
